```java
import java.util.*;

List<String> safe = new ArrayList<>();
safe.add("text");
// safe.add(123);             // compile error - caught now

for (String s : safe) {       // no cast, guaranteed String
    System.out.println(s.length());
}
```
Always supply the type parameter; if you truly need any object, use `List<Object>`, which is still type-checked.

